WEBVTT

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.878
0600 hours.

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:17.212
Regeneration cycle complete.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:23.985
Daily Log, Seven of Nine,
Stardate 15781.2.

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:25.991
Today Ensign Kim and l

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.855
will conduct
a comprehensive diagnostic

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:29.657
of the aft sensor array.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:33.132
L have allocated three hours,
20 minutes for the task

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:34.656
and an additional 17 minutes

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:38.000
for Ensign Kim's usual
conversational digressions.

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.801
L am scheduled to take

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:41.773
a nutritional supplement
at 1500 hours,

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:44.572
engage in one hour
of cardiovascular activity,

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:47.011
then l intend to review a text
the Doctor recommended

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:48.981
entitled A Christmas Carol.

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:51.711
He believes it will have
educational value.

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.082
End log.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.154
L'll get this.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.753
Don't give me
any hints.

00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:06.061
L have no intention
of doing so.

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:08.158
Ensign.

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:09.168
Hi, Seven.

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:10.635
Are you ready to begin

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.194
our sensor diagnostic?

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.796
Ls it 0600 already?

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.967
We've been playing
all night.

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:17.636
Vulcan kal-toh.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:19.736
For a game of logic,

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:21.747
you'd be surprised at
how addictive it is.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.976
Give me a few more minutes
to figure this out.

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:25.847
You should attend
to your duties, Ensign.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.045
L'll accept your forfeit.

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:29.987
No way.

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:32.286
This is the closest
l've ever come to beating you

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:34.259
and l'm not giving up now.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.358
Ahh...

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.665
Impressive.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:50.642
Elementary
spatial harmonics.

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:52.144
Are you ready now?

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:54.373
Yeah. Sure.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.057
L would have
gotten that.

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:10.559
Is there anything
you don't know?

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:11.962
L was Borg.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.498
"L was Borg."

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:14.557
That's what you always say.

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:15.590
But what does it mean?

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:17.967
You have the knowledge
of 10,000 species in your head?

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.868
Not exactly.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:20.964
Each drone's experiences

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:22.907
are processed by
the collective.

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.876
Only useful information
is retained.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:26.276
Still, that
probably makes you

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.177
the most intelligent
human being alive.

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:29.806
Probably.

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.476
So what do you need
the rest of us for?

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:34.479
Forget l asked.

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:37.453
What was that?

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:39.219
We just dropped out of warp.

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:40.954
What's the problem?

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.894
We were hit
by some kind of shock wave.

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:43.953
Source?

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:45.259
Checking.

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:46.925
Hold on.

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:49.127
L just lost
all my sensor readings.

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:51.967
The computer is bringing up
some kind of message,

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:53.267
but l can't access it.

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.137
You better take a look at this.

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:56.369
L can see it.

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:57.671
What is it?

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.008
L have no idea.

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:02.139
My command codes aren't working.

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:05.117
The computer says
l have insufficient clearance

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:06.448
to access the message.

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:10.122
We can't function like this.

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:12.420
L'm going to get Harry up here
to trace the source.

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:14.926
Don't do anything.
L'll take care of this.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.702
Send all sensor data
about the particle wave

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:24.794
to my ready room.

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:27.567
Tom, disengage engines
and hold position here.

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:28.767
Captain...

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:29.832
what's going on?

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:33.535
L can't explain right now.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:36.208
Don't discuss any of this
with the rest of the crew.

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:38.649
L'll have further instructions
for you soon.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.534
Computer, seal the doors
to this room.

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:38.537
No entry
without my authorization.

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:40.596
Doors are sealed.

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:45.907
Access secured data file:
Omega one.

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:48.277
Voiceprint confirmed.

00:05:48.314 --> 00:05:49.804
State clearance code.

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:55.151
Janeway-one-one-five-three-red,
clearance level 10.

00:05:55.187 --> 00:05:56.916
Confirmed.

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:59.857
Sensors have detected
the Omega phenomenon

00:05:59.892 --> 00:06:03.157
within 1.2 light-years
of this vessel.

00:06:03.195 --> 00:06:06.653
Implement the Omega Directive
immediately.

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:09.600
All other priorities
have been rescinded.

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:17.334
Display sensor data.

00:06:20.579 --> 00:06:23.207
L've been informed this is
a highly classified mission.

00:06:23.249 --> 00:06:26.184
Information will be provided
on a need-to-know basis...

00:06:26.218 --> 00:06:27.185
Captain's orders.

00:06:27.219 --> 00:06:29.119
Classified? By who?

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:31.248
We're 60,000 light-years
from Starfleet.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.951
Like l said,
need-to-know.

00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:34.219
B'Elanna, she wants
you to install

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:36.694
multiphasic shielding
around the warp core.

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:39.197
L've never seen
this shield configuration.

00:06:39.231 --> 00:06:41.961
L'd like to run a couple
of computer simulations

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:43.558
- to make sure it's stable.
- No time.

00:06:43.602 --> 00:06:45.593
She needs this
done by 1100 hours.

00:06:45.638 --> 00:06:47.333
1100? L don't think
that's possible.

00:06:47.373 --> 00:06:48.465
Make it possible.

00:06:48.507 --> 00:06:49.906
Are we attempting
to protect

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:52.240
the core from some form
of subspace radiation?

00:06:52.278 --> 00:06:53.245
L don't know
any more than you do.

00:06:53.279 --> 00:06:54.109
It will be difficult

00:06:54.146 --> 00:06:55.977
to complete the task,
without more data.

00:06:56.082 --> 00:06:57.640
The data you've got
will have to do.

00:06:57.683 --> 00:06:59.583
Tom, start modifying
a shuttlecraft

00:06:59.618 --> 00:07:00.744
to withstand extreme

00:07:00.786 --> 00:07:03.516
thermal stress...
12,000 Kelvins at least.

00:07:03.556 --> 00:07:04.523
Aye, sir.

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:05.854
Does all this have
anything to do

00:07:05.891 --> 00:07:08.018
with that secret message
that the Captain received?

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.152
What have
you heard?

00:07:09.195 --> 00:07:10.526
Rumors, mostly.

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:12.087
Janeway's been locked
in her ready room

00:07:12.131 --> 00:07:13.860
for the last 16 hours...

00:07:13.899 --> 00:07:16.925
something about
an Omega Directive.

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:18.163
Omega?

00:07:18.204 --> 00:07:19.171
Ring a bell?

00:07:19.205 --> 00:07:21.673
Look, the speculation
ends right here.

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:23.675
Now, l expect you
to carry out your assignments

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:25.506
with a minimum of gossip,
understood?

00:07:25.544 --> 00:07:26.909
L know it's hard
not to wonder.

00:07:26.946 --> 00:07:28.470
Frankly, l'm
curious myself,

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:30.778
but the Captain was
very adamant about this.

00:07:30.816 --> 00:07:32.579
Get going.

00:07:32.618 --> 00:07:34.483
The Captain
wants to see you.

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:35.612
L thought she might.

00:07:48.033 --> 00:07:49.466
Come in.

00:07:53.105 --> 00:07:55.699
What do you know about
the Omega Directive?

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:57.265
Everything you do,
most likely.

00:07:58.611 --> 00:08:00.636
L thought as much.

00:08:00.679 --> 00:08:03.341
The Borg assimilated
Starfleet Captains.

00:08:03.382 --> 00:08:06.317
You would possess
all of their knowledge.

00:08:06.352 --> 00:08:07.683
That's correct.

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:10.280
Do you intend
to carry out the Directive?

00:08:10.322 --> 00:08:11.584
Yes.

00:08:11.624 --> 00:08:14.821
Then sensors have detected
the molecule.

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:17.920
So it would appear,
but we have to confirm it.

00:08:17.997 --> 00:08:19.157
"We"?

00:08:19.198 --> 00:08:21.393
You're going to help me
carry out the Directive.

00:08:22.601 --> 00:08:23.795
Protocol forbids me

00:08:23.836 --> 00:08:26.430
from discussing this mission
with any of my crew,

00:08:26.472 --> 00:08:28.940
but since you
already know about it,

00:08:29.041 --> 00:08:31.441
my choice is
to either work with you

00:08:31.477 --> 00:08:34.446
or... confine you
to quarters.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:36.846
Perhaps you should
do the latter.

00:08:36.882 --> 00:08:39.214
L will not help
you destroy Omega.

00:08:39.251 --> 00:08:40.912
It should be harnessed.

00:08:40.953 --> 00:08:42.113
That's impossible.

00:08:42.154 --> 00:08:43.644
The Borg believe
otherwise.

00:08:43.689 --> 00:08:45.418
Explain.

00:08:45.458 --> 00:08:47.221
On one occasion,
we were able

00:08:47.259 --> 00:08:49.523
to create a single
Omega molecule.

00:08:49.562 --> 00:08:50.790
We kept it stable

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:52.730
for one-trillionth
of a nanosecond

00:08:52.765 --> 00:08:54.130
before it destabilized.

00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:56.600
We didn't have enough
boronite ore left

00:08:56.635 --> 00:08:59.229
to synthesize more, but
the knowledge we gained

00:08:59.271 --> 00:09:02.434
allowed us to...
refine our theories.

00:09:08.113 --> 00:09:09.273
The Borg have
been waiting

00:09:09.315 --> 00:09:11.374
for the chance
to test them out.

00:09:11.417 --> 00:09:13.180
Yes.

00:09:13.219 --> 00:09:15.278
But we never found
another source of the ore...

00:09:15.321 --> 00:09:16.879
until now.

00:09:20.292 --> 00:09:23.090
Sorry...

00:09:23.128 --> 00:09:26.427
but if someone out there is
experimenting with Omega,

00:09:26.465 --> 00:09:28.490
l'm under orders
to stop them.

00:09:28.534 --> 00:09:31.697
Otherwise, this entire
Quadrant would be at risk.

00:09:31.737 --> 00:09:32.931
Those orders are the result

00:09:33.038 --> 00:09:35.598
of Starfleet's ignorance
and fear.

00:09:35.641 --> 00:09:38.405
L can alleviate your ignorance.

00:09:38.444 --> 00:09:39.411
As for your fear...

00:09:39.445 --> 00:09:40.469
Sometimes fear

00:09:40.513 --> 00:09:42.447
should be respected, Seven.

00:09:42.481 --> 00:09:44.415
Tell me...

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:47.942
how many Borg were sacrificed
during this experiment?

00:09:48.053 --> 00:09:52.217
29 vessels, 600,000 drones,
but that is irrelevant.

00:09:52.258 --> 00:09:54.226
Not to me, not to my crew,

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:55.921
and not to the people
who live in this Quadrant.

00:09:55.961 --> 00:09:57.929
L'm going to neutralize
this threat, Seven,

00:09:57.963 --> 00:09:59.225
with or without your help.

00:10:03.035 --> 00:10:05.401
L will assist you.

00:10:05.437 --> 00:10:06.961
You will?

00:10:07.039 --> 00:10:08.199
L have waited many years

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:09.935
to observe
this molecule firsthand.

00:10:09.975 --> 00:10:13.001
L will not deny myself
that experience.

00:10:15.748 --> 00:10:17.648
All right.

00:10:23.489 --> 00:10:25.252
Go back to your cargo bay.

00:10:25.291 --> 00:10:28.454
Assemble all the data
you have about Omega.

00:10:28.494 --> 00:10:30.758
L'll expect a report
within the hour.

00:10:30.796 --> 00:10:33.287
L didn't realize you had

00:10:33.332 --> 00:10:35.926
such a strong
scientific curiosity.

00:10:35.968 --> 00:10:37.833
Not curiosity...

00:10:37.870 --> 00:10:39.861
desire.

00:10:39.905 --> 00:10:41.532
Desire?

00:10:41.574 --> 00:10:45.533
Omega is infinitely complex,
yet harmonious.

00:10:45.578 --> 00:10:49.241
To the Borg,
it represents perfection.

00:10:49.281 --> 00:10:52.717
L wish to understand
that perfection.

00:10:52.751 --> 00:10:55.311
The Borg's Holy Grail.

00:10:55.354 --> 00:10:56.981
Captain?

00:10:57.022 --> 00:10:59.115
Never mind.

00:10:59.158 --> 00:11:00.921
L'll see you in an hour.

00:11:16.241 --> 00:11:17.640
Arithrazine? What for?

00:11:17.676 --> 00:11:18.973
L'm going on an
away mission.

00:11:19.011 --> 00:11:20.501
What are you
planning to do...

00:11:20.546 --> 00:11:21.945
stroll through
a supernova?

00:11:21.981 --> 00:11:23.243
Something like that.

00:11:23.282 --> 00:11:25.273
20 milligrams... when
can you have it ready?

00:11:25.317 --> 00:11:27.410
Captain, arithrazine is used

00:11:27.453 --> 00:11:28.977
for the most severe cases
of theta

00:11:29.021 --> 00:11:30.579
radiation poisoning.

00:11:30.623 --> 00:11:32.420
A physician must be present
to monitor the treatment.

00:11:32.458 --> 00:11:33.925
That won't be possible.

00:11:33.959 --> 00:11:35.688
Then l'm afraid
l can't accommodate you.

00:11:35.728 --> 00:11:38.322
L'd be in violation
of Starfleet medical protocols.

00:11:38.364 --> 00:11:40.389
Well, l'm overriding
those protocols.

00:11:40.432 --> 00:11:42.764
Don't tell me...

00:11:42.801 --> 00:11:45.770
"The Omega Directive,"
whatever that might be.

00:11:45.804 --> 00:11:47.669
The arithrazine, Doctor.

00:11:49.041 --> 00:11:50.770
It'll be ready in the morning.

00:11:50.809 --> 00:11:51.969
Have it sent to the shuttle bay.

00:11:52.011 --> 00:11:55.344
Captain, l don't know
what's going on here,

00:11:55.381 --> 00:11:58.009
but l'd hate this to be
the last time l ever see you.

00:11:58.050 --> 00:11:59.642
Please be careful.

00:11:59.685 --> 00:12:00.947
L will.

00:12:06.091 --> 00:12:09.527
L've analyzed the sensor logs
using Borg algorithms.

00:12:09.561 --> 00:12:12.428
The shock wave we detected
indicates not one

00:12:12.464 --> 00:12:15.433
but possibly hundreds
of Omega molecules.

00:12:16.535 --> 00:12:17.968
Location?

00:12:18.003 --> 00:12:19.334
Within ten light-years.

00:12:19.371 --> 00:12:21.100
L'm having
difficulty isolating

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:23.131
the exact star system.

00:12:23.175 --> 00:12:24.403
Hundreds of molecules.

00:12:24.443 --> 00:12:25.842
That changes everything.

00:12:25.878 --> 00:12:27.846
A shuttle mission
may be insufficient.

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:30.348
We require the resources
of this entire crew.

00:12:33.018 --> 00:12:34.986
We're going to need
more firepower,

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:37.147
more protection.

00:12:39.258 --> 00:12:41.658
Transfer your data
to the Astrometrics Lab.

00:12:41.694 --> 00:12:43.184
L'll work
on it there.

00:12:44.697 --> 00:12:46.858
Calibration complete.

00:12:46.899 --> 00:12:47.888
Phase modulator.

00:12:51.437 --> 00:12:52.961
Detonator circuits?

00:12:53.005 --> 00:12:54.802
On standby.

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:57.604
We're ready to load
the gravimetric charge.

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:05.375
This looks like enough
for a 50-isoton explosion.

00:13:05.417 --> 00:13:07.385
54, to be exact.

00:13:09.321 --> 00:13:11.312
What are we planning to do,
blow up a small planet?

00:13:11.356 --> 00:13:13.187
L don't know.

00:13:13.225 --> 00:13:14.783
This warhead isn't
standard issue.

00:13:14.827 --> 00:13:16.226
Who designed it, the Captain?

00:13:16.261 --> 00:13:17.694
Mr. Kim, you ask

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:19.425
too many questions.

00:13:19.465 --> 00:13:20.864
Change of plans, gentlemen.

00:13:20.899 --> 00:13:23.333
Increase the charge
to 80 isotons.

00:13:23.368 --> 00:13:24.494
Aye, Captain.

00:13:24.536 --> 00:13:25.594
Harry, when you're done here,

00:13:25.637 --> 00:13:27.662
give B'Elanna a hand
with the shuttlecraft.

00:13:27.706 --> 00:13:28.968
She's reinforcing the hull.

00:13:29.074 --> 00:13:30.268
Right.

00:13:35.447 --> 00:13:38.507
Ensign Hickman thinks
it's Species 8472.

00:13:38.550 --> 00:13:40.450
Pardon me?

00:13:40.486 --> 00:13:41.976
That's his theory.

00:13:42.087 --> 00:13:43.247
There's an opening
in fluidic space

00:13:43.288 --> 00:13:45.313
and Captain Janeway
has to shut it down.

00:13:45.357 --> 00:13:47.757
Want to know what l think?

00:13:47.793 --> 00:13:49.124
No.

00:13:50.929 --> 00:13:54.330
L think there's
a type-6 protostar out there

00:13:54.366 --> 00:13:56.561
and the Captain's planning
on detonating it

00:13:56.602 --> 00:13:57.762
and opening up a wormhole

00:13:57.803 --> 00:13:58.929
to the Alpha Quadrant.

00:13:58.971 --> 00:14:00.233
In theory,
it's possible.

00:14:00.272 --> 00:14:02.035
And because she doesn't
want to get her hopes up,

00:14:02.074 --> 00:14:03.905
she's not telling anybody.

00:14:03.942 --> 00:14:06.240
Then l wouldn't suggest
getting your hopes up.

00:14:07.412 --> 00:14:08.379
Then what do you think it is?

00:14:08.413 --> 00:14:09.380
L do not engage

00:14:09.414 --> 00:14:11.041
in idle speculation.

00:14:11.083 --> 00:14:12.414
Oh, come on, Tuvok.

00:14:12.451 --> 00:14:13.543
Aren't you curious?

00:14:13.585 --> 00:14:16.418
Yes, but we have a task at hand.

00:14:16.455 --> 00:14:18.320
The phase modulator.

00:14:29.268 --> 00:14:31.259
Come in.

00:14:31.303 --> 00:14:33.396
Status report.

00:14:33.438 --> 00:14:34.837
Everything's going
according to schedule.

00:14:34.873 --> 00:14:35.965
Good.

00:14:36.008 --> 00:14:38.977
The Omega Directive doesn't
allow me to say much,

00:14:39.077 --> 00:14:41.068
but l want you to
know what to expect.

00:14:41.113 --> 00:14:43.445
At 0600 hours,
l'll be leaving

00:14:43.482 --> 00:14:45.143
in a shuttle with
Seven of Nine.

00:14:46.518 --> 00:14:48.611
Would it be out of line
to ask where you're going?

00:14:48.654 --> 00:14:50.281
L can tell you this.

00:14:50.322 --> 00:14:52.722
One of two things
is going to happen.

00:14:52.758 --> 00:14:55.359
Either Seven and l will
succeed on our mission

00:14:55.492 --> 00:14:57.119
and return within
a few days,

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:58.991
or your long-range
sensors will detect

00:14:59.096 --> 00:15:01.587
a large explosion
in subspace.

00:15:01.631 --> 00:15:03.792
If that occurs, you'll
have less than ten seconds

00:15:03.834 --> 00:15:06.132
to jump to warp and
get the hell out of here.

00:15:06.169 --> 00:15:08.933
Head for the Alpha Quadrant
and don't look back. Understood?

00:15:10.707 --> 00:15:11.935
L always thought that Starfleet

00:15:11.975 --> 00:15:14.170
was run
by duty-crazed bureaucrats,

00:15:14.211 --> 00:15:15.940
but l find it hard to believe
that even they

00:15:16.046 --> 00:15:18.571
would order a Captain
to go on a suicide mission.

00:15:18.615 --> 00:15:21.607
This shuttle excursion
is your idea, isn't it?

00:15:23.086 --> 00:15:27.045
Let's just say
l've had to amend the Directive,

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:28.921
given the circumstances.

00:15:28.959 --> 00:15:31.519
But you have your orders
and l expect you to follow them.

00:15:31.561 --> 00:15:33.119
That's expecting a lot.

00:15:33.163 --> 00:15:37.099
You're asking me to abandon
my Captain and closest friend

00:15:37.134 --> 00:15:38.829
without even telling me why.

00:15:38.869 --> 00:15:40.063
If it were
a simple matter of trust,

00:15:40.103 --> 00:15:41.764
l wouldn't hesitate to tell you.

00:15:43.173 --> 00:15:44.731
But we've encountered situations

00:15:44.775 --> 00:15:47.676
where information
was taken from us by force.

00:15:47.711 --> 00:15:50.976
L can't allow knowledge of Omega
to go beyond Voyager.

00:15:51.047 --> 00:15:52.947
That's a reasonable argument,

00:15:52.983 --> 00:15:54.814
but you're not always
a reasonable woman.

00:15:54.851 --> 00:15:57.877
You're determined
to protect this crew

00:15:57.921 --> 00:16:00.116
and this time,
you've taken it too far.

00:16:00.157 --> 00:16:02.648
A dangerous mission...
fine, l'll acknowledge that...

00:16:02.692 --> 00:16:04.216
but isn't it more
likely to succeed

00:16:04.261 --> 00:16:06.593
with everyone behind you,
working together?

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:08.598
Ordinarily, l'd agree,

00:16:08.632 --> 00:16:11.430
but this Directive was issued
many years ago.

00:16:11.468 --> 00:16:14.767
Starfleet didn't exactly have
our predicament in mind, did it?

00:16:14.805 --> 00:16:18.036
Lost in the Delta Quadrant
with no backup.

00:16:18.074 --> 00:16:21.475
L can't ignore the orders,

00:16:21.511 --> 00:16:24.071
but l won't ask the crew
to risk their lives

00:16:24.114 --> 00:16:25.513
because of my obligation.

00:16:25.549 --> 00:16:27.107
"My obligation."

00:16:27.150 --> 00:16:28.947
That's where you're wrong.

00:16:28.985 --> 00:16:31.351
Voyager may be alone out here,
but you're not.

00:16:31.388 --> 00:16:33.583
Let us help you.

00:16:33.623 --> 00:16:35.181
We'll keep
classified information

00:16:35.225 --> 00:16:36.749
limited to the senior staff.

00:16:36.793 --> 00:16:39.125
We'll take
every security precaution.

00:16:39.162 --> 00:16:42.290
Just don't try to do this alone.

00:16:50.607 --> 00:16:52.404
Assemble the troops.

00:16:57.047 --> 00:16:58.605
If we were in
the Alpha Quadrant right now,

00:16:58.648 --> 00:17:00.513
we wouldn't be having
this conversation.

00:17:00.550 --> 00:17:02.882
L'd be in contact
with Starfleet Command

00:17:02.919 --> 00:17:04.409
and they'd send in
a specialized team

00:17:04.454 --> 00:17:05.921
to deal with the crisis.

00:17:05.956 --> 00:17:08.424
In their absence, we're
going to have to make do

00:17:08.458 --> 00:17:09.584
with the training
l've received

00:17:09.626 --> 00:17:10.615
and the knowledge

00:17:10.660 --> 00:17:13.094
Seven of Nine has
retained from the Borg.

00:17:15.098 --> 00:17:17.430
You've all seen
this symbol.

00:17:17.467 --> 00:17:21.130
Omega... the last letter
of the Greek alphabet...

00:17:21.171 --> 00:17:22.638
chosen by Starfleet

00:17:22.672 --> 00:17:24.572
to represent a threat
not only to the Federation

00:17:24.608 --> 00:17:26.667
but to the entire galaxy.

00:17:26.710 --> 00:17:29.679
Only starship captains
and Federation flag officers

00:17:29.713 --> 00:17:32.204
have been briefed
on the nature of this threat.

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:36.710
What you're about to hear will
not go beyond these bulkheads.

00:17:36.753 --> 00:17:37.777
Is that clear?

00:17:40.524 --> 00:17:41.821
Good.

00:17:53.003 --> 00:17:54.630
This is Omega.

00:17:54.671 --> 00:17:56.662
A molecule?

00:17:56.706 --> 00:17:59.072
Not just any molecule...

00:17:59.109 --> 00:18:02.101
the most powerful substance
known to exist.

00:18:02.145 --> 00:18:03.908
A single Omega molecule

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:07.074
contains the same energy
as a warp core.

00:18:07.117 --> 00:18:10.848
In theory, a small chain of them
could sustain

00:18:10.887 --> 00:18:11.854
a civilization.

00:18:11.888 --> 00:18:13.378
The molecule was
first synthesized

00:18:13.423 --> 00:18:14.515
over a hundred years ago

00:18:14.558 --> 00:18:17.686
by a Starfleet physicist
named Ketteract.

00:18:17.727 --> 00:18:21.322
L think he was hoping to develop
an inexhaustible power source.

00:18:21.364 --> 00:18:22.831
Or a weapon.

00:18:22.866 --> 00:18:24.731
Ketteract managed to synthesize

00:18:24.768 --> 00:18:29.228
a single molecule particle
of Omega,

00:18:29.272 --> 00:18:31.797
but it only existed
for a fraction of a second

00:18:31.841 --> 00:18:33.741
before it destabilized.

00:18:36.947 --> 00:18:42.408
This was a classified research
center in the Lantaru Sector.

00:18:42.452 --> 00:18:44.079
Ketteract and 126

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:46.645
of the Federation's
leading scientists

00:18:46.690 --> 00:18:48.885
were lost in the accident.

00:18:48.925 --> 00:18:51.894
Rescue teams
attempting to reach the site

00:18:51.928 --> 00:18:53.759
discovered an unexpected

00:18:53.797 --> 00:18:55.697
secondary effect.

00:18:55.732 --> 00:18:57.529
There were
subspace ruptures

00:18:57.567 --> 00:19:00.866
extending out
several light-years.

00:19:00.904 --> 00:19:03.702
The Lantaru Sector...

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:06.368
it's impossible to create
a stable warp field there.

00:19:06.409 --> 00:19:08.843
You can only fly through
it at sublight speeds.

00:19:08.878 --> 00:19:11.642
But l was always told that it
was a natural phenomenon.

00:19:11.681 --> 00:19:13.478
You're saying it was caused

00:19:13.516 --> 00:19:15.416
by a single molecule
of this stuff?

00:19:15.452 --> 00:19:17.716
Omega destroys subspace.

00:19:17.754 --> 00:19:21.281
A chain reaction
involving a handful of molecules

00:19:21.324 --> 00:19:24.623
could devastate subspace
throughout an entire Quadrant.

00:19:24.661 --> 00:19:26.925
If that were to happen,

00:19:26.963 --> 00:19:29.557
warp travel
would become impossible.

00:19:29.599 --> 00:19:31.760
Spacefaring civilization
as we know it

00:19:31.801 --> 00:19:33.928
would cease to exist.

00:19:33.970 --> 00:19:36.404
When Starfleet realized
Omega's power,

00:19:36.439 --> 00:19:38.066
they suppressed
all knowledge of it.

00:19:38.108 --> 00:19:39.541
Have you detected
Omega here

00:19:39.576 --> 00:19:41.476
in the Delta Quadrant?

00:19:41.511 --> 00:19:42.808
L'm afraid so.

00:19:44.914 --> 00:19:46.347
L've been authorized to use

00:19:46.383 --> 00:19:49.045
whatever means necessary
to destroy it.

00:19:49.085 --> 00:19:51.212
Tom, l've calculated

00:19:51.254 --> 00:19:53.245
the location of the molecules.

00:19:53.289 --> 00:19:55.348
L'll transfer the coordinates
to the helm.

00:19:55.392 --> 00:19:57.257
Take us there at full impulse.

00:19:57.293 --> 00:19:58.817
Aye, Captain.

00:19:58.862 --> 00:20:01.387
L don't have to tell you
what's at stake.

00:20:01.431 --> 00:20:05.367
If a large-scale
Omega explosion occurs,

00:20:05.402 --> 00:20:08.963
we will lose the ability
to go to warp forever.

00:20:09.039 --> 00:20:10.768
We've got our work

00:20:10.807 --> 00:20:11.967
cut out for us.

00:20:25.388 --> 00:20:28.983
Captain's Log, supplemental.
Encrypt log entry.

00:20:29.092 --> 00:20:30.684
We're approaching
the star system

00:20:30.727 --> 00:20:32.422
where we believe
we'll find Omega.

00:20:32.462 --> 00:20:34.987
L have to admit,
l've never been

00:20:35.031 --> 00:20:36.896
this apprehensive
about a mission.

00:20:36.933 --> 00:20:40.266
L know how Einstein must have
felt about the atom bomb,

00:20:40.303 --> 00:20:42.931
or Marcus when she developed
the Genesis Device.

00:20:42.972 --> 00:20:44.940
They watched helplessly
as science

00:20:44.974 --> 00:20:46.874
took a destructive course,

00:20:46.910 --> 00:20:49.777
but l have the chance
to prevent that from happening.

00:20:49.813 --> 00:20:51.371
L just hope it's not too late.

00:20:51.414 --> 00:20:52.938
Status report?

00:20:52.982 --> 00:20:55.780
This is a harmonic
resonance chamber.

00:20:55.819 --> 00:20:58.481
The Borg designed it
to contain and stabilize Omega.

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:02.558
L thought l asked you to
work on the photon torpedo.

00:21:02.592 --> 00:21:04.719
The torpedo may be
insufficient.

00:21:04.761 --> 00:21:07.958
L can modify this chamber
to emit an inverse frequency.

00:21:08.031 --> 00:21:11.398
It will be enough to dissolve
Omega's interatomic bonds.

00:21:16.339 --> 00:21:18.136
Here's to Borg ingenuity.

00:21:18.174 --> 00:21:20.108
This is excellent
work, Seven.

00:21:20.143 --> 00:21:22.077
We may need this.

00:21:22.112 --> 00:21:23.602
The modifications require

00:21:23.646 --> 00:21:24.943
several complex
calculations.

00:21:24.981 --> 00:21:26.744
Assist me.

00:21:26.783 --> 00:21:28.717
L guess l will.

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:31.917
L'm curious...

00:21:31.955 --> 00:21:33.980
when did the Borg
discover Omega?

00:21:34.023 --> 00:21:35.991
229 years ago.

00:21:36.025 --> 00:21:37.652
Assimilation?
Yes.

00:21:37.694 --> 00:21:39.389
Of 13 different species.

00:21:39.429 --> 00:21:40.657
Thirteen?

00:21:41.698 --> 00:21:43.757
Lt began with Species 262.

00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:45.631
They were primitive,
but their oral history

00:21:45.668 --> 00:21:47.659
referred to
a powerful substance

00:21:47.704 --> 00:21:49.228
which could "burn the sky."

00:21:49.272 --> 00:21:53.299
The Borg were intrigued...
which led them to Species 263.

00:21:53.343 --> 00:21:54.503
They, too, were primitive

00:21:54.544 --> 00:21:57.138
and believed it was a drop
of blood from their creator.

00:21:57.180 --> 00:21:58.272
Fascinating.

00:21:58.314 --> 00:22:00.009
Yes, but irrelevant.

00:22:00.049 --> 00:22:02.779
We followed this trail of myth
for many years

00:22:02.819 --> 00:22:04.810
until finally
assimilating a species

00:22:04.854 --> 00:22:06.481
with useful scientific data.

00:22:06.523 --> 00:22:08.491
We then created
the molecule ourselves.

00:22:08.525 --> 00:22:11.255
Omega caused
quite a stir

00:22:11.294 --> 00:22:12.955
among my own species.

00:22:13.062 --> 00:22:15.496
Federation cosmologists
had a theory...

00:22:15.532 --> 00:22:19.696
that the molecule
once existed in nature...

00:22:19.736 --> 00:22:22.671
for an infinitesimal period
of time

00:22:22.705 --> 00:22:25.265
at the exact moment
of the big bang.

00:22:25.308 --> 00:22:28.277
Some claimed Omega
was the primal source of energy

00:22:28.311 --> 00:22:30.905
for the explosion
that began our universe.

00:22:30.947 --> 00:22:32.744
A creation myth, like any other.

00:22:32.782 --> 00:22:34.147
Perhaps.

00:22:34.184 --> 00:22:36.709
What is it the Borg say?

00:22:36.753 --> 00:22:38.414
That Omega is perfect?

00:22:38.454 --> 00:22:39.751
Yes.

00:22:39.789 --> 00:22:42.417
Is that a theory or a belief?

00:22:42.458 --> 00:22:44.289
Bridge to Captain.

00:22:44.327 --> 00:22:45.316
Go ahead.

00:22:45.361 --> 00:22:47.124
We're approaching
the coordinates.

00:22:47.163 --> 00:22:48.425
L'm on my way.

00:22:48.464 --> 00:22:50.625
L'm leaving this project
in your hands.

00:22:50.667 --> 00:22:53.534
Use whatever resources
and personnel you need.

00:22:53.570 --> 00:22:54.559
Understood.

00:23:02.178 --> 00:23:03.645
We've entered a
planetary system.

00:23:03.680 --> 00:23:04.669
Inhabited?

00:23:04.714 --> 00:23:06.204
There's a pre-warp
civilization

00:23:06.249 --> 00:23:07.546
on the outermost planet.

00:23:07.584 --> 00:23:09.677
The source of Omega
seems to be further in.

00:23:09.719 --> 00:23:12.381
The damage to subspace
in this region is extreme.

00:23:12.422 --> 00:23:14.219
We won't be able
to go to warp.

00:23:16.426 --> 00:23:17.916
We are encountering distortions.

00:23:17.961 --> 00:23:19.121
Track their origin.

00:23:19.162 --> 00:23:21.494
An M-Class moon.

00:23:21.531 --> 00:23:22.964
We're in visual range.

00:23:23.032 --> 00:23:24.624
On screen.

00:23:26.269 --> 00:23:27.964
There is a subnucleonic reaction

00:23:28.071 --> 00:23:30.130
occurring
in the upper atmosphere.

00:23:30.173 --> 00:23:31.265
It is apparently emanating

00:23:31.307 --> 00:23:32.934
from a structure
on the moon's surface.

00:23:32.976 --> 00:23:34.705
Can your sensors
penetrate the atmosphere?

00:23:34.744 --> 00:23:35.733
Stand by.

00:23:36.412 --> 00:23:38.642
My God.

00:23:38.681 --> 00:23:39.670
Over 300,000

00:23:39.716 --> 00:23:41.809
square kilometers...
destroyed.

00:23:41.851 --> 00:23:44.843
Scan the structure.

00:23:44.888 --> 00:23:47.789
Are there any Omega
molecules remaining?

00:23:47.824 --> 00:23:49.416
L can't tell.

00:23:49.459 --> 00:23:52.485
Several sections of the outpost
are still shielded.

00:23:52.528 --> 00:23:53.859
L'm detecting life signs.

00:23:53.897 --> 00:23:54.795
How many?

00:23:54.831 --> 00:23:55.798
A few dozen, maybe.

00:23:55.832 --> 00:23:57.424
It's hard to get
a clear reading.

00:23:57.467 --> 00:23:59.332
Harry, can we transport
to the surface?

00:23:59.369 --> 00:24:00.802
L can get you there,

00:24:00.837 --> 00:24:02.634
but conditions in the structure
aren't good.

00:24:02.672 --> 00:24:04.238
There are high levels
of radiation.

00:24:04.371 --> 00:24:05.736
Tuvok...

00:24:05.772 --> 00:24:08.036
assemble a rescue team

00:24:08.075 --> 00:24:11.533
and have them report to Sick Bay
for arithrazine inoculations.

00:24:11.578 --> 00:24:13.944
Tell the Doctor to
prepare for casualties.

00:24:13.981 --> 00:24:16.245
Tom, move Voyager
into a high orbit

00:24:16.283 --> 00:24:17.580
and then join
the away team.

00:24:17.618 --> 00:24:18.642
We'll need a field medic.

00:24:18.685 --> 00:24:20.118
Yes, ma'am.

00:24:20.153 --> 00:24:21.518
You're going with them?

00:24:21.555 --> 00:24:24.251
Lf Omega's still down there,
l have to find it.

00:24:24.291 --> 00:24:26.122
L'll keep an open com-link
with the ship.

00:24:26.159 --> 00:24:27.592
You have the Bridge.

00:24:46.446 --> 00:24:48.971
L'm picking up
Omega's resonance frequency.

00:24:49.016 --> 00:24:52.281
It's here,
but l can't pinpoint a location.

00:24:57.190 --> 00:24:58.452
L need to ask you questions

00:24:58.492 --> 00:25:01.325
about the experiments
you've been conducting here.

00:25:01.361 --> 00:25:05.024
There was... an accident.

00:25:07.434 --> 00:25:09.925
We lost containment.

00:25:10.037 --> 00:25:11.937
The substance you were
trying to create...

00:25:11.972 --> 00:25:15.339
did any of it
survive the explosion?

00:25:15.375 --> 00:25:16.342
Yes.

00:25:16.376 --> 00:25:17.400
Where?

00:25:20.480 --> 00:25:23.813
Inside the primary
test chamber.

00:25:27.754 --> 00:25:29.585
- Who are you?
- Captain Janeway

00:25:29.623 --> 00:25:31.318
of the Starship Voyager.

00:25:31.358 --> 00:25:32.655
We're here to help you.

00:25:32.693 --> 00:25:34.786
Away team to Voyager.
Two to beam

00:25:34.828 --> 00:25:35.795
directly to Sick Bay.

00:25:35.829 --> 00:25:36.887
Aye, Captain.

00:25:39.099 --> 00:25:41.567
This door is solid duritanium

00:25:41.601 --> 00:25:42.898
13 centimeters thick.

00:25:42.936 --> 00:25:43.960
Can we get it open?

00:25:44.037 --> 00:25:45.061
The duritanium
has melted

00:25:45.105 --> 00:25:46.834
into the door frame.

00:25:46.873 --> 00:25:48.807
We'll need to cut
through the metal with phasers.

00:25:48.842 --> 00:25:49.866
Do it.

00:25:49.910 --> 00:25:50.968
Captain...

00:25:51.011 --> 00:25:52.535
l'd be negligent
if l didn't point out

00:25:52.579 --> 00:25:55.207
that we are about to violate
the Prime Directive.

00:25:55.248 --> 00:25:56.772
For the duration
of this mission,

00:25:56.817 --> 00:25:58.444
the Prime Directive
is rescinded.

00:25:58.485 --> 00:25:59.975
Let's get this over with.

00:26:11.832 --> 00:26:14.824
Crewman Dell,
l'm assigning you a task

00:26:14.868 --> 00:26:16.597
more suited
to your abilities.

00:26:16.636 --> 00:26:19.935
Calibrate the ionic-pressure
seals on the observation ports.

00:26:20.040 --> 00:26:22.440
Your new designation
is Three of Ten.

00:26:22.476 --> 00:26:23.465
Yes, ma'am.

00:26:33.420 --> 00:26:36.321
L've got more isolinear
processors for you to install.

00:26:36.356 --> 00:26:37.653
Thanks,

00:26:37.691 --> 00:26:39.659
but l need to get the power
relays on line first.

00:26:39.693 --> 00:26:41.684
Are you sure
that's a good idea?

00:26:41.728 --> 00:26:43.753
Ensign Wildman
was assigned to that.

00:26:43.797 --> 00:26:45.424
This is ridiculous.

00:26:45.465 --> 00:26:46.432
L'm not going
to waste time

00:26:46.466 --> 00:26:48.161
just because Seven
wants to turn this team

00:26:48.201 --> 00:26:49.498
into her own
private collective.

00:26:49.536 --> 00:26:51.436
She says
it's more efficient.

00:26:51.471 --> 00:26:52.961
Maybe for a
bunch of drones.

00:26:56.843 --> 00:26:58.970
Six of Ten, this is
not your assignment.

00:26:59.079 --> 00:27:01.445
Please, stop
calling me that.

00:27:01.481 --> 00:27:04.177
You are compromising
our productivity.

00:27:07.220 --> 00:27:09.688
L am reassigning you
to chamber maintenance.

00:27:09.723 --> 00:27:12.556
Your new designation
is Two of Ten.

00:27:14.161 --> 00:27:17.426
Wait a minute.
You're demoting me?

00:27:17.464 --> 00:27:19.523
Since when do the Borg
pull rank?

00:27:19.566 --> 00:27:21.466
A Starfleet protocol l adapted.

00:27:21.501 --> 00:27:23.492
L find it most useful.

00:27:23.537 --> 00:27:26.028
L'm glad you're not the Captain.

00:27:28.809 --> 00:27:29.833
How's it coming?

00:27:29.876 --> 00:27:30.934
The crew can be
quite efficient

00:27:31.044 --> 00:27:32.636
when properly organized.

00:27:32.679 --> 00:27:34.840
The harmonic chamber will be
completed within the hour.

00:27:34.881 --> 00:27:35.870
Good.
L'll let the Captain know.

00:27:35.916 --> 00:27:36.883
Has she
retrieved

00:27:36.917 --> 00:27:37.941
any new data from the surface?

00:27:38.051 --> 00:27:39.211
Not yet.

00:27:39.252 --> 00:27:40.549
They're still trying to access

00:27:40.587 --> 00:27:41.679
the primary test chamber.

00:27:41.721 --> 00:27:42.745
Were there survivors?

00:27:42.789 --> 00:27:45.053
A few. The Doctor's
treating them in Sick Bay.

00:27:47.527 --> 00:27:48.516
Commander.

00:27:51.431 --> 00:27:53.365
Seven's taking this
"hive mentality"

00:27:53.400 --> 00:27:54.924
just a little too far.

00:27:54.968 --> 00:27:56.765
Designated functions,
numbered drones...

00:27:56.803 --> 00:27:57.770
l wouldn't be surprised

00:27:57.804 --> 00:27:59.499
if she started plugging
us into alcoves.

00:27:59.539 --> 00:28:02.997
When in the collective,
Harry... adapt.

00:28:18.725 --> 00:28:20.920
Which of them is the
senior researcher?

00:28:21.027 --> 00:28:22.927
This gentleman.
Why do you ask?

00:28:22.996 --> 00:28:25.260
He has knowledge
l require.

00:28:25.298 --> 00:28:26.925
He also happens to be
barely conscious.

00:28:26.967 --> 00:28:27.934
Come back in an hour.

00:28:27.968 --> 00:28:28.935
Unacceptable.

00:28:29.002 --> 00:28:30.196
Unavoidable.

00:28:30.237 --> 00:28:31.204
This is my Sick Bay.

00:28:31.238 --> 00:28:32.432
The man needs to recover.

00:28:32.472 --> 00:28:33.564
The Captain left me

00:28:33.607 --> 00:28:35.666
in charge of our
efforts on Voyager.

00:28:35.709 --> 00:28:36.676
L would be negligent

00:28:36.710 --> 00:28:38.678
if l ignored a new
source of information.

00:28:45.218 --> 00:28:48.278
Our next social skills
seminar is entitled

00:28:48.321 --> 00:28:51.757
"Adding Diplomatic Flair
to Future Negotiations."

00:28:56.029 --> 00:28:57.428
How are you feeling, sir?

00:28:58.832 --> 00:29:00.959
Better. Thank you.

00:29:01.001 --> 00:29:05.131
Are you comfortable enough
to speak with this individual?

00:29:07.507 --> 00:29:09.498
Keep it brief.

00:29:13.980 --> 00:29:16.175
How many of the molecules
were you able

00:29:16.216 --> 00:29:17.547
to synthesize?

00:29:17.584 --> 00:29:20.280
200 million?

00:29:20.320 --> 00:29:21.844
L'm not certain.

00:29:21.888 --> 00:29:24.516
What is the iso-frequency
of your containment field?

00:29:24.558 --> 00:29:26.924
1.68 terahertz.

00:29:26.960 --> 00:29:28.655
We used the molecule's

00:29:28.695 --> 00:29:30.822
own resonance
to calculate the field.

00:29:30.864 --> 00:29:32.991
That should've been enough
to stabilize them.

00:29:34.200 --> 00:29:35.861
Obviously it wasn't.

00:29:35.902 --> 00:29:39.804
Obviously,
but your approach is innovative.

00:29:39.839 --> 00:29:43.366
Perhaps l can adapt your
technique and improve upon it.

00:29:43.410 --> 00:29:45.207
You will assist me.

00:29:48.882 --> 00:29:52.147
Our equipment was destroyed.

00:29:52.185 --> 00:29:57.487
If you can transfer
the molecules to your ship...

00:29:57.524 --> 00:29:59.617
maybe they can be saved.

00:29:59.659 --> 00:30:01.957
L have no intention
of saving them.

00:30:01.995 --> 00:30:03.622
What?

00:30:03.663 --> 00:30:06.632
My orders are to destroy
the Omega molecules.

00:30:06.666 --> 00:30:10.124
This is my life's work...
the salvation of my people.

00:30:10.170 --> 00:30:11.398
Will you assist me or not?

00:30:11.438 --> 00:30:14.965
Our resources are nearly gone.

00:30:15.008 --> 00:30:18.535
The future of my people
depends on this discovery!

00:30:18.578 --> 00:30:20.307
Then your answer is no.

00:30:21.948 --> 00:30:24.610
Small-minded creatures.

00:30:24.651 --> 00:30:27.984
You destroy whatever
you don't understand!

00:30:29.522 --> 00:30:31.649
Rescue ships are on the way.

00:30:31.691 --> 00:30:33.921
They won't let you do it.

00:30:35.462 --> 00:30:37.453
Please, try
to be calm.

00:30:37.497 --> 00:30:39.089
Seven, you'll
have to leave.

00:30:42.335 --> 00:30:44.667
You don't realize
what you're doing.

00:30:44.704 --> 00:30:48.834
You don't know what this is...
what this means...

00:30:48.875 --> 00:30:50.638
On the contrary.

00:30:51.845 --> 00:30:53.642
L understand perfectly.

00:31:15.735 --> 00:31:17.930
We've disabled
the locking mechanism.

00:31:17.971 --> 00:31:20.064
Narrow your phaser beams to
cut through the inner seal.

00:31:20.106 --> 00:31:21.073
Inadvisable.

00:31:21.107 --> 00:31:22.836
We'd risk penetrating
the containment field.

00:31:26.146 --> 00:31:27.636
Then we'll have to use
some elbow grease.

00:31:27.681 --> 00:31:28.841
Give me a hand.

00:31:30.650 --> 00:31:31.639
Oh.

00:31:36.156 --> 00:31:37.384
Right.

00:31:54.574 --> 00:31:57.008
There's enough here
to wipe out subspace

00:31:57.110 --> 00:31:58.737
across half the Quadrant.

00:31:58.778 --> 00:32:01.246
L'll order the away
teams back to Voyager,

00:32:01.281 --> 00:32:03.875
and target this facility
with a gravimetric charge.

00:32:03.917 --> 00:32:04.941
It won't be enough.

00:32:04.984 --> 00:32:07.077
We'll have to go
with our Borg option.

00:32:07.120 --> 00:32:08.246
Ensign.

00:32:08.288 --> 00:32:09.448
Yes, Captain.

00:32:09.489 --> 00:32:11.218
Return to the ship.

00:32:11.257 --> 00:32:12.656
Tell Commander Chakotay

00:32:12.692 --> 00:32:14.956
to help Seven complete
the harmonic chamber.

00:32:17.230 --> 00:32:19.562
We'll have to transport Omega
directly to the ship.

00:32:19.599 --> 00:32:20.623
That means finding a way

00:32:20.667 --> 00:32:22.191
to shut down
this containment field.

00:32:22.235 --> 00:32:24.328
It's unfortunate
we can't study

00:32:24.370 --> 00:32:26.463
this phenomenon
in more detail.

00:32:26.506 --> 00:32:27.973
We may not have the
opportunity again.

00:32:28.041 --> 00:32:29.941
Let's hope we never do.

00:32:29.976 --> 00:32:33.139
A curious statement
from a woman of science.

00:32:33.179 --> 00:32:35.943
L'm also a woman who
occasionally knows when to quit.

00:32:38.218 --> 00:32:40.482
Take another look
at your tricorder.

00:32:43.123 --> 00:32:44.818
Omega's too dangerous.

00:32:44.858 --> 00:32:48.589
L won't risk half the Quadrant
to satisfy our curiosity.

00:32:48.628 --> 00:32:51.188
It's arrogant
and it's irresponsible.

00:32:56.569 --> 00:32:58.537
The final frontier
has some boundaries

00:32:58.571 --> 00:33:00.129
that shouldn't be crossed...

00:33:01.608 --> 00:33:03.337
and we're looking at one.

00:33:04.811 --> 00:33:06.870
We don't need to destroy
the molecules.

00:33:06.913 --> 00:33:08.505
L believe l've found a way
to stabilize them.

00:33:08.548 --> 00:33:11.142
The alien in Sick Bay
calibrated

00:33:11.184 --> 00:33:13.482
his containment field using
Omega's own resonance...

00:33:13.520 --> 00:33:15.511
an approach unknown
to the Borg.

00:33:15.555 --> 00:33:16.886
L have modified
this chamber...

00:33:16.923 --> 00:33:18.618
Those weren't
your orders.

00:33:18.658 --> 00:33:20.455
The Captain wants
Omega eliminated.

00:33:22.262 --> 00:33:23.820
That is still an option

00:33:23.863 --> 00:33:27.060
if she insists on
yielding to her fear.

00:33:28.601 --> 00:33:29.829
Show me what you've done.

00:33:31.838 --> 00:33:33.829
This simulation
shows the molecules

00:33:33.873 --> 00:33:36.637
in their free state,
highly unstable.

00:33:36.676 --> 00:33:39.975
L've modified the chamber
to emit a harmonic wave form

00:33:40.046 --> 00:33:41.843
that will dampen
the molecules.

00:33:41.881 --> 00:33:45.715
Looks great in theory,
but this is only a simulation.

00:33:45.752 --> 00:33:47.049
How are you going to test it?

00:33:48.721 --> 00:33:50.154
On Omega.

00:33:51.691 --> 00:33:53.181
Bad idea.

00:33:53.226 --> 00:33:55.854
One mistake and no one will
be around for a second try.

00:33:55.895 --> 00:33:57.260
It will work.

00:33:57.297 --> 00:33:58.628
Someday, maybe.

00:33:58.665 --> 00:33:59.996
Hang on to your research.

00:34:00.099 --> 00:34:01.896
For now, we stick to the plan.

00:34:01.935 --> 00:34:03.402
Stand by to transport

00:34:03.436 --> 00:34:06.372
the molecules into this chamber
and neutralize them as ordered.

00:34:06.505 --> 00:34:09.872
L have been a member
of this crew for nine months.

00:34:09.908 --> 00:34:10.932
In all of that time,

00:34:11.043 --> 00:34:13.204
l have never made
a personal request.

00:34:13.245 --> 00:34:15.440
L am making one now.

00:34:15.481 --> 00:34:16.880
Allow me to proceed.

00:34:18.384 --> 00:34:20.215
Please.

00:34:20.252 --> 00:34:23.346
Why is this so important to you?

00:34:26.492 --> 00:34:28.926
Particle zero-one-zero...

00:34:28.961 --> 00:34:31.953
the Borg designation
for what you call Omega.

00:34:32.064 --> 00:34:34.225
Every drone is aware
of its existence.

00:34:34.266 --> 00:34:37.429
We were instructed
to assimilate it at all costs.

00:34:37.469 --> 00:34:40.836
It is...

00:34:40.873 --> 00:34:42.431
perfection.

00:34:42.474 --> 00:34:46.433
The molecules exist
in a flawless state...

00:34:46.478 --> 00:34:49.970
infinite parts
functioning as one.

00:34:50.082 --> 00:34:51.572
Like the Borg.

00:34:53.519 --> 00:34:55.680
Precisely.

00:34:55.721 --> 00:34:59.487
L am no longer Borg,

00:34:59.525 --> 00:35:02.824
but l still need to understand
that perfection.

00:35:02.861 --> 00:35:06.024
Without it, my existence
will never be complete.

00:35:10.969 --> 00:35:13.836
Commander,
you are a spiritual man.

00:35:13.872 --> 00:35:15.499
That's right.

00:35:15.541 --> 00:35:20.535
If you had the chance to see
your God, your Great Spirit,

00:35:20.579 --> 00:35:23.013
what would you do?

00:35:24.616 --> 00:35:27.744
L'd pursue it...
with all my heart.

00:35:27.786 --> 00:35:30.448
Then you understand.

00:35:30.489 --> 00:35:32.957
L think l do.

00:35:33.058 --> 00:35:36.357
L'll inform the Captain
of your discovery.

00:35:36.395 --> 00:35:39.990
For now, her orders stand.

00:35:41.834 --> 00:35:43.358
Thank you.

00:35:59.218 --> 00:36:02.483
Set the confinement beam
to its narrowest dispersion.

00:36:02.521 --> 00:36:03.545
Understood.

00:36:03.589 --> 00:36:06.752
We'll target this facility
with the gravimetric torpedo.

00:36:06.792 --> 00:36:08.817
If anything goes wrong
during transport,

00:36:08.861 --> 00:36:10.385
that'll be our only hope.

00:36:10.429 --> 00:36:12.090
Bridge to Janeway.

00:36:12.130 --> 00:36:14.496
We've detected two ships
on an intercept course.

00:36:14.533 --> 00:36:16.626
They're not responding to hails.

00:36:16.668 --> 00:36:18.067
How long until they get here?

00:36:18.103 --> 00:36:19.536
Less than four
minutes, Captain.

00:36:19.571 --> 00:36:20.697
Stand by to transport

00:36:20.739 --> 00:36:22.832
the molecules directly
to the harmonic chamber.

00:36:22.875 --> 00:36:24.638
Understood.
Bridge to Cargo Bay.

00:36:24.676 --> 00:36:26.337
Yes, Commander.

00:36:26.378 --> 00:36:27.470
Seven, get ready.

00:36:27.513 --> 00:36:28.912
We'll have to do this quickly.

00:36:28.947 --> 00:36:30.414
That's not advisable.

00:36:30.449 --> 00:36:31.416
We don't have a choice.

00:36:31.450 --> 00:36:32.883
The alien ships
are on their way.

00:36:32.918 --> 00:36:34.317
Then l recommend moving the ship

00:36:34.353 --> 00:36:36.480
within 5,000 kilometers
of the surface.

00:36:36.522 --> 00:36:38.581
That'll take us
right into the atmosphere.

00:36:38.624 --> 00:36:40.353
With our shields down,
we won't be able to withstand

00:36:40.392 --> 00:36:42.952
the thermal reaction
for more than a few seconds.

00:36:43.061 --> 00:36:44.460
Then we'll only get one shot
at this.

00:36:44.496 --> 00:36:45.554
Take us in.

00:36:45.597 --> 00:36:47.258
Aye, sir.

00:36:47.299 --> 00:36:48.698
Transporter status?

00:36:48.734 --> 00:36:50.429
Targeting scanners are locked.

00:36:50.469 --> 00:36:51.731
Captain, are you ready?

00:36:52.738 --> 00:36:54.603
Pattern enhancers are active.

00:36:54.640 --> 00:36:55.538
Do it.

00:36:55.574 --> 00:36:56.905
We're 11,000 kilometers

00:36:56.942 --> 00:36:58.068
from the surface.

00:36:58.110 --> 00:37:00.340
If we get much closer,
we'll incinerate.

00:37:00.379 --> 00:37:01.744
We're losing
structural integrity.

00:37:01.780 --> 00:37:03.213
9,000 Kilometers.

00:37:03.248 --> 00:37:04.613
We're close enough.

00:37:04.650 --> 00:37:05.776
Energize.

00:37:05.817 --> 00:37:07.375
Initiating transport.

00:37:11.957 --> 00:37:14.084
The Omega molecules are stable.

00:37:14.126 --> 00:37:16.424
Transport was successful.

00:37:16.461 --> 00:37:18.691
L've got the away team
in Transporter Room 2.

00:37:18.730 --> 00:37:20.322
Get us out of here,
maximum impulse.

00:37:20.365 --> 00:37:21.662
Already on it.

00:37:21.700 --> 00:37:22.860
How far away are those ships?

00:37:22.901 --> 00:37:25.233
They're right on our tail.

00:37:35.948 --> 00:37:38.280
We're heading
into an area of open space...

00:37:38.317 --> 00:37:40.547
no indications of life
or any kind of technology.

00:37:40.586 --> 00:37:42.213
We can carry out
the procedure

00:37:42.254 --> 00:37:43.812
with no risk
to anyone else.

00:37:43.855 --> 00:37:45.413
Except those two ships
behind us.

00:37:45.457 --> 00:37:46.446
Can we stay
ahead of them?

00:37:46.491 --> 00:37:47.651
Not for long.

00:37:47.693 --> 00:37:49.786
How soon can we clear
the subspace ruptures

00:37:49.828 --> 00:37:50.795
and go to warp?

00:37:50.829 --> 00:37:52.421
Ten, maybe 15 minutes,

00:37:52.464 --> 00:37:54.796
but those ships will catch up
to us before then.

00:37:54.833 --> 00:37:57.393
Well, we have one advantage.
We've got Omega.

00:37:57.436 --> 00:37:58.926
They won't risk
firing at us.

00:37:58.971 --> 00:38:00.836
At least not until they've
run out of options.

00:38:00.872 --> 00:38:01.896
That should
give us a chance

00:38:02.007 --> 00:38:03.133
to neutralize
the molecules.

00:38:03.175 --> 00:38:04.836
Captain, we might have
another problem.

00:38:04.876 --> 00:38:06.400
Seven of Nine?

00:38:06.445 --> 00:38:08.913
She's convinced she
can stabilize Omega.

00:38:08.947 --> 00:38:10.812
L thought
we'd settled that question.

00:38:10.849 --> 00:38:12.476
While you were on the surface,
she showed me

00:38:12.517 --> 00:38:14.576
a pretty convincing simulation
of how it could be done.

00:38:14.620 --> 00:38:17.054
L should've known
she wouldn't just let this go.

00:38:17.089 --> 00:38:18.283
L'll be in Cargo Bay 2.

00:38:27.432 --> 00:38:28.899
Seven, the procedure?

00:38:28.934 --> 00:38:29.923
Lt's working.

00:38:30.035 --> 00:38:32.435
11 percent Of the molecules
have already been neutralized.

00:38:32.471 --> 00:38:34.132
Let's see if we can speed
up the process a little.

00:38:34.172 --> 00:38:36.333
Did Commander Chakotay
tell you about my idea?

00:38:36.375 --> 00:38:37.535
Yes.

00:38:37.576 --> 00:38:39.066
Then you will allow me

00:38:39.111 --> 00:38:41.045
to stabilize
the remaining molecules.

00:38:41.079 --> 00:38:42.341
You know l can't do that.

00:38:43.548 --> 00:38:45.846
Your Starfleet Directive
is no longer relevant.

00:38:45.884 --> 00:38:47.681
L have found a way
to control Omega.

00:38:47.719 --> 00:38:49.914
L don't care if you can
make it sing and dance.

00:38:49.955 --> 00:38:51.149
We're getting rid of it.

00:38:52.257 --> 00:38:53.281
A foolish decision.

00:38:53.325 --> 00:38:55.486
Yes, but it's mine to make.
Now, step aside.

00:38:58.764 --> 00:39:01.232
L could've done this
without your permission,

00:39:01.266 --> 00:39:04.360
but l chose to follow
your command structure.

00:39:05.704 --> 00:39:07.797
L should've made the attempt.

00:39:07.839 --> 00:39:10.000
L still can.

00:39:10.042 --> 00:39:11.168
But you won't.

00:39:13.879 --> 00:39:17.280
You know l'm not trying to stop
you from finding perfection,

00:39:17.315 --> 00:39:21.012
but l can't risk the
safety of this Quadrant.

00:39:21.053 --> 00:39:24.921
Omega must end here.
We both know that.

00:39:38.837 --> 00:39:40.327
Status?

00:39:40.372 --> 00:39:42.135
18 percent.

00:39:42.174 --> 00:39:43.732
This could take hours.

00:39:43.775 --> 00:39:46.107
Can you increase the
harmonic resonance?

00:39:46.144 --> 00:39:47.543
Yes, but it would rupture
the chamber.

00:39:49.614 --> 00:39:52.082
How many molecules
would we neutralize?

00:39:52.117 --> 00:39:53.846
40, 50 percent at best.

00:39:55.353 --> 00:39:57.116
That's good enough.

00:39:57.155 --> 00:39:59.555
Our torpedo
can take care of the rest.

00:39:59.591 --> 00:40:00.751
Janeway to Bridge.

00:40:00.792 --> 00:40:02.054
Chakotay here.

00:40:02.094 --> 00:40:03.925
Chakotay, l want you
to clear Deck 4.

00:40:03.962 --> 00:40:06.954
Put emergency force fields
around this section.

00:40:07.065 --> 00:40:09.590
Prepare to decompress
Cargo Bay 2 on my command.

00:40:09.634 --> 00:40:10.601
Understood.

00:40:10.635 --> 00:40:13.229
Tuvok, load
the gravimetric torpedo.

00:40:13.271 --> 00:40:16.707
Once we've jettisoned
the chamber, fire.

00:40:16.742 --> 00:40:17.709
Aye, Captain.

00:40:17.743 --> 00:40:19.608
Harmonic resonance to maximum.

00:40:26.184 --> 00:40:27.310
Commander, they're
closing on us.

00:40:27.352 --> 00:40:28.319
They're attempting

00:40:28.353 --> 00:40:29.945
to stop us with a tractor beam.

00:40:29.988 --> 00:40:31.615
Adjust shields to compensate.

00:40:31.656 --> 00:40:32.588
They're hailing us.

00:40:32.624 --> 00:40:33.591
On screen.

00:40:34.159 --> 00:40:35.524
Disengage your engines

00:40:35.560 --> 00:40:37.118
and prepare to be boarded.

00:40:37.162 --> 00:40:38.254
L can't do that.

00:40:38.296 --> 00:40:40.890
You've stolen our technology,

00:40:40.932 --> 00:40:42.399
abducted our people.

00:40:42.434 --> 00:40:43.401
Your people are safe.

00:40:43.435 --> 00:40:44.868
They're receiving medical care.

00:40:44.903 --> 00:40:46.962
L'll be glad to get them
back to you when this is over,

00:40:47.005 --> 00:40:48.939
but we're keeping the molecules.

00:40:48.974 --> 00:40:51.568
L won't allow this substance
to fall into enemy hands.

00:40:51.610 --> 00:40:53.009
L'll destroy it first.

00:40:53.111 --> 00:40:54.476
They're charging weapons.

00:40:54.513 --> 00:40:55.980
You'll destabilize
the molecules.

00:40:56.014 --> 00:40:57.003
We'll both
be destroyed.

00:40:57.115 --> 00:41:00.448
Then return
our technology... now!

00:41:00.485 --> 00:41:02.953
L'm sorry.
That's not possible.

00:41:09.795 --> 00:41:12.195
Direct hit.
Shields down ten percent.

00:41:12.230 --> 00:41:14.198
Evasive maneuvers.
Try to shake them off.

00:41:16.201 --> 00:41:18.226
Harmonic resonance
at maximum, Captain.

00:41:18.270 --> 00:41:19.259
The molecules?

00:41:19.304 --> 00:41:20.828
80 percent remaining.

00:41:20.872 --> 00:41:22.499
We need to get that
down to 60.

00:41:23.975 --> 00:41:25.966
Any damage to our
power grid could

00:41:26.077 --> 00:41:28.102
overload the chamber...
Omega would chain-react.

00:41:28.146 --> 00:41:29.670
The same thought
crossed my mind.

00:41:31.016 --> 00:41:31.983
Where are we now?

00:41:32.017 --> 00:41:33.882
72 percent.

00:41:33.919 --> 00:41:34.886
That's close enough.

00:41:34.920 --> 00:41:36.649
Bridge, start
the decompression sequence.

00:41:36.688 --> 00:41:37.916
Acknowledged.

00:41:39.324 --> 00:41:40.757
What's wrong?
What's happening?

00:41:40.792 --> 00:41:42.987
The molecules
are stabilizing.

00:41:43.094 --> 00:41:44.391
What?

00:41:44.429 --> 00:41:45.396
L've done nothing.

00:41:45.430 --> 00:41:46.556
It's occurring
spontaneously.

00:41:46.598 --> 00:41:47.895
That's impossible.

00:41:49.801 --> 00:41:52.395
Decompression in 30 seconds.

00:41:54.439 --> 00:41:57.636
Decompression in 25 seconds.

00:41:57.676 --> 00:42:00.008
Seven, let's move!

00:42:00.078 --> 00:42:03.047
Decompression in 20 seconds.

00:42:03.081 --> 00:42:04.844
Seven.

00:42:04.883 --> 00:42:07.579
Decompression in 15 seconds.

00:42:09.554 --> 00:42:12.421
Decompression in ten seconds.

00:42:12.457 --> 00:42:14.084
Tom, are we clear
of the subspace ruptures?

00:42:14.125 --> 00:42:15.092
Almost.

00:42:15.126 --> 00:42:16.855
L need maximum warp
within ten seconds

00:42:16.895 --> 00:42:18.419
or we'll be stuck
at ground zero.

00:42:18.463 --> 00:42:19.896
Yes, sir.

00:42:19.931 --> 00:42:21.558
Decompression is complete.

00:42:21.600 --> 00:42:23.727
The harmonic chamber
has been jettisoned.

00:42:23.768 --> 00:42:25.395
Fire.

00:42:33.712 --> 00:42:36.579
We made it.
We're at warp 1.

00:42:38.550 --> 00:42:39.881
The alien ships?

00:42:39.918 --> 00:42:41.180
Out of range.

00:42:41.219 --> 00:42:42.413
Tuvok?

00:42:42.454 --> 00:42:44.922
Sensors show no traces
of Omega molecules.

00:42:54.332 --> 00:42:56.357
Mission accomplished.

00:43:12.751 --> 00:43:17.051
Captain's Log,
Stardate 51793.4.

00:43:17.088 --> 00:43:19.283
We've arranged
for our guests in Sick Bay

00:43:19.324 --> 00:43:21.292
to be taken back
to their homeworld,

00:43:21.326 --> 00:43:24.227
and we can finally
put this mission behind us.

00:43:24.262 --> 00:43:26.059
This will be
my last encrypted log

00:43:26.097 --> 00:43:28.088
concerning the Omega Directive.

00:43:28.133 --> 00:43:31.159
The classified data files
will now be destroyed.

00:43:35.206 --> 00:43:37.106
L wondered who was
running my program.

00:43:37.142 --> 00:43:40.441
Master da Vinci doesn't like
visitors after midnight.

00:43:40.478 --> 00:43:43.538
He protested.
L deactivated him.

00:43:43.581 --> 00:43:45.742
What're you
doing here, Seven?

00:43:45.784 --> 00:43:50.483
This simulation contains...
many religious components.

00:43:50.522 --> 00:43:52.319
L was studying them

00:43:52.357 --> 00:43:55.986
to help me understand
what l saw in Cargo Bay 2.

00:43:56.061 --> 00:43:58.552
The data wasn't clear
on why Omega

00:43:58.596 --> 00:44:01.793
stabilized in the last few
seconds, but chances are

00:44:01.833 --> 00:44:06.133
it was simply a chaotic anomaly,
nothing more.

00:44:06.171 --> 00:44:09.140
For 3.2 seconds...

00:44:09.174 --> 00:44:11.972
l saw perfection.

00:44:14.779 --> 00:44:20.240
When Omega stabilized,
l felt a curious sensation.

00:44:20.285 --> 00:44:24.051
As l was watching it,
it seemed to be watching me.

00:44:36.101 --> 00:44:38.592
The Borg have
assimilated many species

00:44:38.636 --> 00:44:42.732
with mythologies to explain
such moments of clarity.

00:44:42.774 --> 00:44:45.937
L've always dismissed
them as trivial.

00:44:48.880 --> 00:44:50.245
Perhaps l was wrong.

00:44:55.220 --> 00:44:57.017
If l didn't
know you better...

00:44:58.990 --> 00:45:03.017
l'd say you just had
your first spiritual experience.
